  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> be an identity, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>s</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> are constants, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
